If the current branch ref file doesn't exist (common when refs are packed and no loose ref is present yet), watchFile() returns undefined and no branch watcher is installed. In that state, new commits on the current branch typically won't touch .git/HEAD or packed-refs, so git state changes can be missed entirely. Consider adding a fallback watcher (e.g., watch the refs/heads directory or retry installing the branch watcher on 'rename'/packed-refs events) so commits are still detected when the ref file is created later.
